 "transcript": [
  "[action] The eldest son returns from a trip with Pear Blossom.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung stands and stares at his son.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"It is a good thing and I am proud of it,\"",
  "[action] The eldest son stands with his back to his father.",
  "[silence] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung says nothing.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung looks at his son with amazement.",
  "[action] The eldest son eats and looks at his father with indifference.",
  "[says] The eldest son discusses a new boat with his father.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"It is a great boat and it will be well worth the money.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and it is better to be safe than sorry,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"But tell me, my son, what is the meaning of this, that you do not know the price of a little boat that will carry two men? Is it a thing I should know or not?\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"I could buy a boat that would carry twenty men and I did not know the price of a little boat that would carry two,\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and you are a great merchant!\"",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"I am and I will be a great merchant,\"",
  "[action] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung pats his son's cheek",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and now I will tell you the price of a little boat,\"",
  "[says] Wang Lung tells his son the price of a little boat.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"It is about a hundred dollars.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Now you see that it is worth something.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the second son): \"Now I have heard of a man who sells his land and buys his son a good education. It is a different thing to buy a son a good education and to buy him a little boat.\""
 ],
